The presentation of Claude Code tool calls and permission prompts over the
Agent Client Protocol (tool titles and kinds, diff content for edits, the
"allow once / allow always / reject" options, `_meta.claudeCode.toolName`)
follows the mapping of the official Node adapter:

  @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp
  https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

No code from that adapter, and no code from the Claude Agent SDK, is copied
here. The `claude` headless stream-json protocol was implemented from
observation of the Claude Code CLI (version 2.1.287) and its public CLI
reference.

Dependencies (Rust crates, linked into the binary):
  agent-client-protocol 2.2.0 and agent-client-protocol-schema 1.9.1
    (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/rust-sdk
  futures, serde, serde_json, uuid, schemars, derive_more, strum, tracing
    and their dependencies: MIT, Apache-2.0, or MIT OR Apache-2.0
    (memchr: Unlicense OR MIT; unicode-ident, build time only:
    (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0). See Cargo.lock.

